  "text": "\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n2026 City of Salix Special Election (August 18, 2026) - Elections - Woodbury County, Iowa\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n Skip to content\n \n\n \n\n \n Woodbury County\n Iowa • Elections\n \n \n\n \n\n Facebook Contact Us\n \n \n\n \n \nVote \n \n \nRegister to Vote\n \nAbsentee Voting\n \nMaps\n \nMilitary/Overseas Voting\n \nPrecincts\n \nVoter ID\n \n \n \nElections \n \n \nUpcoming Elections\n \nPast Elections\n \nSample Ballots\n \nPrecinct Election Officials\n \nTypes of Elections\n \n \n \nElected Officials \n \n \nFederal\n \nState\n \nCounty\n \nCity\n \nSchool Board\n \nTownship\n \nDrainage\n \n \n \nCandidates\n \nNews\n \nFAQ\n \n \n \n\n \n\n\n\n\n Woodbury County\nElections\n\n\n\n Due to staffing and security needs, the ballot drop box is no longer in use. Voted ballots can be returned by mail or in person to 620 Douglas St, Rm 103. Other Election News & Satellite Locations \n\n\n\n\n \n\n \nElections 2026 City of Salix Special Election\n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n \nElections by Year\n\n \n2026 \n2025 \n2024 \n2023 \n2022 \n2021 \n2020 \n2019 \n2018 \n2017 \n2016 \n2015 \n2014 \n2013 \n2012 \n2011 \n2010 \nView All\n\n\nElections\n\n \nUpcoming Elections\n \nPast Elections\n \nSample Ballots\n \nPrecinct Election Officials\n \nTypes of Elections\n \nCentral Committee Bylaws\n\n \n \n\n \n2026 City of Salix Special Election\n\n \nAugust 18, 2026\n Special Election \n \n\n A Special Election is any election that is not regularly scheduled. A special election may be held for any purpose authorized or required by law; often to fill a vacancy or for a public measure. \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \nVoter Turnout\n\n \n\n \nRegistered\n \n\n \n230\n \n\n \nVoted\n \n\n\n26.1%\n \n60\n \n\n \n\n \n\n\n \n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n \n \nArchived Election Details\n A special election will be held on Tuesday, August 18, 2026, to fill a vacancy on the Salix City Council. All eligible electors residing within the City of Salix are eligible to vote. \nVoters can find their specific precinct and polling location by entering their address on our Find Your Polling Place page. \n \n\nCandidate Filing Information \n \n\nThe candidate filing window is currently open. To qualify for the ballot, candidates must meet the following criteria and deadlines: \n \n \n \nEligibility: Candidates must be eligible electors living in the City of Salix both at the time of filing nomination papers and at the time of the election. \n \nRequirements: Candidates must file a Nomination Petition and an Affidavit of Candidacy. \n \nSignature Requirement: Nomination Petition must have a minimum of 10 Precinct 33 eligible voter signatures. \n \nFiling Deadline: All completed nomination papers must be submitted to the County Auditor’s Office (620 Douglas St, Rm 103, Sioux City) no later than Friday, July 24, 2026, at 5:00 PM. \n \n \n\nThree Ways to Vote \n \n\nVoters have three options to cast their ballot for this special election: \n \n\n1. Vote by Mail (Absentee Ballot) \n \n \n \nRequest Window: Eligible voters may request a mail-in absentee ballot from now through Monday, August 3, 2026, at 5:00 PM. \n \nMailing Date: Ballots requested early will begin mailing on Wednesday, July 29, 2026. \n \nHow to Request: \n \n \nBy Phone: Call the Woodbury County Auditor’s Office at 712-279-6465 to request a form by mail. Note: The request must be made verbally by the eligible voter themselves. \n \nOnline/Print: Download and print the official application form from the Secretary of State Office website. \n \n \n \nSubmission: Return completed and signed request forms by mail or in person to: \n \n \n\nWoodbury County Auditor\n \n620 Douglas St, Rm 103\n \nSioux City, IA 51101 \n \n\n2. Early In-Person Voting \n \n \n \nDates & Times: Wednesday, July 29 through Monday, August 17, 2026 (Monday through Friday, 8:00 AM – 4:30 PM). \n \nLocation: Woodbury County Courthouse, Auditor’s Office (620 Douglas St, Rm 103, Sioux City). \n \n \n\n3. Election Day Voting \n \n \n \nDate & Times: Tuesday, August 18, 2026, from 7:00 AM to 8:00 PM. \n \nLocation: Eligible voters residing in Precinct 33 (Salix) must vote at Salix City Hall, 319 Tipton Street. Precinct 33 is the only precinct participating in this special election. \n \n \n\nFor More Information \n \n\nFor additional details regarding candidate filing or voting procedures, please contact the Woodbury County Elections Division at 712-279-6465. \n \n \n\n \n \nSample Ballots (PDF)\n Search Ballots by Precinct Number or Township\n \n\n Sample Ballot\n \n \n \n\n \nBack: Past Elections\n \n \n\n\n\n\n\nThis webpage was printed on October 17, 2026. For the most current election-related information, visit the Woodbury County, Iowa, Elections website at https://elections.woodburycountyiowa.gov.\n\n\n\n \n\n Woodbury County Courthouse\n\n 620 Douglas St. - Room 103\n \nSioux City, IA 51101\n\n Contact Us\n\n Accessibility\n\n Woodbury County Website\n \n \nOffice Hours\n\n Monday - Friday\n \n8AM - 4:30PM \n \nContact Information\n\n Phone: (712) 279-6465\n \nFax: (712) 2796629 \n \n\n \n\n Facebook Contact Us\n \n\n \n \n\n\n\n\n \npowered by \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n"
